  "title": "Timothy Helton",
  "creator": "CrossFit",
  "description": "A team-of-three workout: a 2,364 m row, ten rounds of 49 wall balls, 26 pull-ups, a 200 m run, 8 ring muscle-ups and 40 deadlifts, then each team member builds to a heavy single back squat. Honours Timothy Helton, a U.S. Army and Tennessee National Guard Kiowa Warrior pilot who died in 2024 of cancer linked to deployment exposures. The numbers encode his life; split the work so one athlete moves at a time.",
